<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Live Equivocation ~ the one attack detection cannot fix, built last

The federated-mesh collision (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision`>> #the-mesh-field) named the roadmap's biggest exposure. This meme holds it OPEN for later work — the outside negentropy to gather, the fiction stories to run, and the ruling the operator leans toward (pull recovery-quorum FORWARD beside the sensorium).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-two-thieves`>>

!! Two thieves, and they differ

* ''The DEAD-key thief'' breaks a drawer and finds a key you STOPPED using. ''KERI pre-rotation already defeats them'' — the key they hold cannot authorize its own succession; you rotated past it. The FACE rung handles this.
* ''The LIVING-key thief'' captures your key WHILE YOU STILL SIGN WITH IT — a compromised phone, a coerced signature, a shared cabal-name one member turns. Now ''two of you present one name in real time,'' and both hold a valid key. KERI states plainly: a live current+next capture has ''NO administrative recovery from keys alone.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-blind-spot`>>

!! Detection and recovery each sit in the other's blind spot

The sensorium ''DETECTS'' the equivocation — it sees two of you. But ''seeing it does not RESTORE you'': you stand as a name with two valid claimants and no key-only way to prove which one holds true. Only ''recovery'' — a trusted quorum re-keying you under a fresh root — puts you back. And worse: a living thief who ALSO controls enough carriage can make the ambient itself lie (the diffusion-sensing fool — a well-connected corner reads as "the whole mesh moved"), so ''abstain fires and detection goes blind EXACTLY during the live attack.'' Detection cannot fix what it sees; recovery cannot act on what it cannot see. ''Built apart, the living hijack has neither in time.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-human-stakes`>>

!! Who this serves (the irl tension)

The journalist who loses a source-protecting identity to seizure under duress. The activist whose shared movement-name a defector turns. The family cabal one compromised device betrays. For all of them, ''detection that only says "there are two of you" gives a diagnosis with no cure.'' Recovery beside detection — a quorum that re-keys the moment a watcher sees the equivocation — gives the cure, and it must ''already stand when the attack lands,'' not built two milestones later.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/elyncia-as-qa`>>

!! Elyncia serves as the first QA world (fiction as the harness)

Real cabals with real stakes do not exist yet, so abstract unit tests cannot feel the tension the mechanics must survive. ''The fiction serves as the first QA environment.'' Telarus the wild-mage lit Elyncia's DreamNet ~500 years before modern day (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/telarus`>>), and 500 years of rise · dormancy · revival · betrayal · inheritance give a scenario library to RUN the mechanics against. A cabal name grafted across generations; a wild-mage's DreamNet identity live-hijacked mid-working; a shrine-realm slept a century then woken for a rite; a Dread-Pirate-Roberts-style name presented by a rotating crew — each makes a load-bearing user story for the ahi-kā reading, the handle-KEL, the recovery-quorum, and this exposure. The `AHI_KA_500YR` defaults (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ahi-ka`>>) stand calibrated to this world; tune them by running its events. ''irl tension + fiction series = the QA env.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed to later spirits (the research queue)

# ''Outside negentropy'' — collide the live-equivocation case against the field: KERI/vLEI live-key recovery ceremonies, threshold re-keying (FROST resharing), social-recovery wallets (Argent, safe-guardians), duress/coercion-resistant schemes (deniable keys, canaries), MPC custody rotation. What does anyone deployed do when a key gets stolen WHILE ALIVE?
# ''Fiction user stories'' — mine the Elyncia canon for concrete hijack/inheritance/dormancy scenarios and render each as a QA vector against the mechanics.
# ''The ruling'' — the operator leans PULL RECOVERY-QUORUM FORWARD beside the sensorium (co-design detection + recovery). A later pass confirms the sequence and the recovery-rotation ⊥ equivocation-fork distinction a watcher must draw. See the code seam `packages/lararium-mesh/src/recovery-registration.ts` and <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/after-the-seat`>> (`W30`).
# ''ANSWERED at primary source — the recovery-field survey.'' No deployed or researched system recovers from a fully live key capture using key material alone; the residual (an attacker holding current+next, or a full threshold within one epoch, ''acting inside the window'') holds universally. KERI states it: "there is no recovery mechanism once the keys for the root control authority have been fully captured," and its superseding-rule A1 (a non-delegated rotation cannot supersede another rotation) makes a root-level live capture terminal. ONLY a ''time-lock + veto window'' touches a genuinely live key, deployed everywhere: did:plc's priority-ordered rotation keys + a ''72-hour window'' in which a colder higher-authority key rewrites history, clobbering the lower-authority key; Nostr NIP-41's pre-committed successor + OpenTimestamps anchor + a ''30-day public contest window''; social-recovery wallets' guardian time-lock+veto (Argent 36h, Safe 28d) — which confirm the civic keel (''the recovery quorum and the impersonation quorum stand as ONE quorum''). Duress schemes (GrapheneOS wipe, LUKS-nuke, hidden volumes) only ''destroy or signal, never rotate an already-copied key'', and all fall to observe-first suppression — a duress key denies future access or raises an alarm; it does not recover you. The residual stays inherent, not a shortfall to engineer away.
# ''CONSTRUCTIVE — CHURP makes the GRAFT a share-refresh, bounding the living-thief window on the FROST tier.'' CHURP (Maram et al., eprint 2019/017) performs dynamic-committee proactive secret sharing: at each handoff the committee re-shares so ''shares from epoch //e// become useless in epoch //e+1//, while the secret and its public key stay unchanged'', with members joining/leaving and threshold //t// changing at the handoff — mechanism-for-mechanism the GRAFT (`mintHandleGraft` rolls the owner-set + threshold, `prefix`/`handleKeyDid` fixed). The built k-of-n runs as a MULTISIG (`graftSigs` gathers //t// distinct Ed25519 signatures), with no shared secret to refresh; CHURP earns its keep only on the ''FROST/veiled-Circle branch'' (the-veil-ladder), where a private Circle signs as ONE invisible key — there a captured share ''dies at the next graft, public handle key unchanged, no rotation visible on the wire.'' A scheduled graft cadence, paced by FfzClock to the adversary's measured creep, then serves as a proactive-refresh interval. Take the ''OFF-CHAIN construction only'' — CHURP's dispute path resolves on-chain; route accusation to the duplicity-proof + veto (`detectDuplicity`, `foldPersonaContests`), never a chain. The residual stays inherent: PSS refreshes a STANDING secret and does nothing once an adversary holds ≥//t// shares WITHIN one epoch (they reconstruct) — it shrinks the window, it does not close the simultaneous-quorum seizure the two-thieves already name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-decides-it`>>

!! What this path needs before anyone can rule it (operator, 2026-09-13)

''The PULL-FORWARD lean stands SET ASIDE — not the plan.'' Sequencing recovery-quorum construction beside
the sensorium reads reasonable and rests on nothing measured. The path DEFERS until the infrastructure
stands to test it, and defers cleanly: nothing downstream waits on it, and the residual it addresses
(§#/owed) reads as ''inherent'' rather than as a shortfall anyone fails to engineer away.

!!! The one number that decides the shape

''Only a time-lock + veto window touches a genuinely live key'' (§#/owed, answered at
primary source). Every deployed system picks a duration — did:plc 72 hours, Nostr NIP-41 30 days, Argent
36 hours, Safe 28 days — and ''a window shorter than the time a watcher takes to NOTICE plays as theatre'': the
thief acts, nobody contests in time, and the ceremony ratifies the capture while looking rigorous.

So the ruling waits on ''measured detection latency'': how long, in practice, between a duplicity landing
on a board and a watcher folding it into a contest. Nobody has measured it, because the organ that would
measure it does not stand.

!!! What must stand first, and what each one buys

# ''A fully running sensorium stack.'' The detection half. `detectDuplicity` folds a proof, but no
live plane WATCHES for one across real traffic — detection latency has no observer, so its distribution
has no sample. With the stack up, the number becomes an experiment rather than an estimate.
# ''A fully set-up meshpalace.'' The memory half. A latency distribution wants HISTORY, not one reading:
the window must clear the tail, never the median, and only a durable telemetry plane holds enough
observations to see a tail at all.

''Both, together, answer one question'': what window clears the observed detection tail with margin? That
number picks the mechanism — a short window suits an automatic priority-key clobber (did:plc's shape), a
long one suits a public contest (NIP-41's shape), and the two want different code.

!!! What a later pass should NOT re-derive

''The residual stays inherent.'' An adversary holding current+next, or a full threshold inside one epoch,
acting within the window, defeats every deployed scheme — KERI states it outright. A pass that arrives
hoping to close that hole will spend itself; the work lies in BOUNDING the window, never closing it.

''CHURP bounds the FROST branch and only that branch'' (§#/owed): it earns its keep where a private Circle
signs as one invisible key, and buys nothing against the built multisig graft, which holds no shared secret
to refresh.

<<~/ahu>>

